8,8,6,8,8,6,8,8,8,8,8,8]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"Each blue (colour 1) object in these grids is a 5×5 hollow square frame. In the outputs, a magenta (colour 6) cross is drawn through the centre of every frame.\n\n**How the outputs are built**\n- For each frame, find its centre cell: the middle of its bounding box.\n- Paint colour 6 along the entire row and the entire column through that centre, running from one grid border to the other.\n- Only background cells (8) change. The frame cells (1) stay as they are, so the lines look as if they pass \"under\" the walls.\n\n**Checking against the demonstrations**\n- **Pair 2** has one frame with bbox rows 1–5 and columns 3–7, so its centre is (3,5).\n  - Row 3 becomes `6 6 6 1 6 6 6 1 6 6 6 6 6 6 6`.\n  - Column 5 is 6 everywhere except at the two frame walls (rows 1 and 5).\n  - This accounts for exactly the 25 changed cells.\n- **Pair 1** has two frames, with centres (5,5) and (11,10).\n  - Its output has full lines at rows 5 and 11 and at columns 5 and 10.\n  - Where lines from different frames cross on background, the cell is simply 6. For example, (5,10) is 6 in the output.\n  - All 48 changes are 8→6, which matches the four lines minus the frame cells.\n\n**The test input**\n- The frames have centres (3,8) and (11,5).\n- So the program fills rows 3 and 11 and columns 8 and 5 with 6 wherever the cell is 8.\n- The program emits one stage per frame (its cross added), then the final grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    for o in objs:\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        cy, cx = (y0 + y1) // 2, (x0 + x1) // 2\n        row = out[cy]\n        row[g[cy] == bg] = 6\n        col = out[:, cx]\n        col[g[:, cx] == bg] = 6\n        emit(out, f\"Draw colour-6 lines across row {cy} and column {cx} through the centre of the frame at {o['box']}, only over background.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final grid: every frame has a full cross through its centre.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- For each frame, find its centre cell: the middle of its bounding box."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"d06c05a16390145fc9b9b9c3ee1bec14df2aacc94fab02f8549cd711f388476f","task_sha256":"a372f5d722266745a70e13d2492223619e85331eb9468fd651f490559b278c88","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
